    "field": "Urban climate",
    "problem": "State-of-the-art climate models underestimate urban heat wave risks because they largely lack urban representation, thereby failing to account for model structural uncertainty, which is a dominant source of variability in projections.",
    "method": "The paper proposes an urban climate emulator, trained on a single Earth System Model with urban physics, to generate global multi-model urban heat wave projections by applying it to atmospheric outputs from various climate models that lack urban representation, thereby quantifying model structural uncertainty.",
    "task": "The task is to project future urban heat waves globally and quantify the associated model structural uncertainty using an urban climate emulator combined with large ensemble global climate simulations.",
